```ts
import type { GeospatialCamera } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function tiltGlobeCamera(camera: GeospatialCamera, pitch: number): void {
  // Allow full pitch at every radius, including the fully zoomed-out start radius.
  camera.limits.pitchDisabledRadiusScale = null;

  // Only the pitch changes, so yaw, radius, and center are preserved.
  camera.pitch = pitch;
}
```

I disabled the radius-dependent pitch clamp and then wrote the requested pitch, preserving the camera’s yaw, radius, and center. I assumed the library’s `pitch` convention matches your stated one (0 = straight down); if it were measured from the horizon, the angle would need to be complemented.
